# Kanban Board API — NestJS

Backend API for a Kanban Board application, built with [NestJS](https://nestjs.com/).

## Table of Contents

- [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)
- [Installation](#installation)
- [Environment Configuration](#environment-configuration)
- [Running the Project](#running-the-project)
- [Startup Error Handling](#startup-error-handling)
- [VTB Developer CLI](#vtb-developer-cli)
- [API Routes](#api-routes)
- [Swagger](#swagger)
- [Project Structure](#project-structure)

## Prerequisites

- Node.js v18 or v20
- npm
- PostgreSQL

Check installed versions:

```bash
node -v
npm -v
```

## Installation

```bash
npm install
```

## Environment Configuration

The project uses a `.env` and `.env.doker`file at the root for configuration.

Copy the example file and fill it in:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Create a `.env.docker` file at the root of the project and define the following environment variables:

| Variable       | Description                        |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `DB_HOST`      | PostgreSQL database host           |
| `DB_PORT`      | PostgreSQL database port           |
| `DB_USERNAME`  | PostgreSQL database username       |
| `DB_PASSWORD`  | PostgreSQL database password       |
| `DB_DATABASE`  | PostgreSQL database name           |
| `DATABASE_URL` | PostgreSQL database connection URL |

## Running the Project

### Development mode

```bash
npm run start:dev
```

### Production mode

```bash
npm run build
npm run start:prod
```

Once started, the server responds on the port configured via `PORT` (defaults to `http://localhost:3000`).

## Startup Error Handling

The project validates critical environment variables at startup (via a `Joi` validation schema integrated with `@nestjs/config`).

- **Nominal case**: all required variables are set → the server starts normally and responds on the configured port.
- **Error case**: a critical variable (e.g. `DATABASE_URL`) is missing or invalid → startup fails immediately with an explicit error message naming the variable at fault, rather than a silent crash or an unreadable low-level error.

Example message shown when a variable is missing:

```
Error: Config validation error: "DATABASE_URL" is required
```
## VTB Developer CLI
The project includes a custom PowerShell CLI to simplify common development commands. All custom CLI commands must be prefixed with vtb.
The CLI provides shortcuts for Node.js, npm, Docker, and NestJS commands.

```
vtb <command>
```

## API Routes

All API routes are prefixed with /api.

**Authentication & Users**

| Method  | Route                | Description                                         | Authentication       | Response                                   |
| ------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `POST`  | `/api/auth/register` | Register a new user                                 | No                   | `201 Created` + user without `password`    |
| `POST`  | `/api/auth/login`    | Login a user                                        | No                   | `200 OK` + JWT `accessToken`               |
| `GET`   | `/api/users/me`      | Get the currently authenticated user                | Yes                  | `200 OK` + user without `password`         |
| `PATCH` | `/api/users/{id}`    | Update user information, including role/permissions | Yes + owner or admin | `200 OK` + updated user without `password` |

**Lists**

| Method   | Route             | Description                        | Authentication | Response                     |
| -------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `GET`    | `/api/lists`      | Get the authenticated user's lists | Yes            | `200 OK` + array of lists    |
| `POST`   | `/api/lists`      | Create a new list                  | Yes            | `201 Created` + created list |
| `PATCH`  | `/api/lists/{id}` | Update a list                      | Yes + owner    | `200 OK` + updated list      |
| `DELETE` | `/api/lists/{id}` | Delete a list                      | Yes + owner    | `204 No Content`             |



## Swagger

Once the server is running, interactive Swagger documentation is available at:

```
http://localhost:3000/api
```

All API endpoints (users, lists, cards) are listed there and can be tested directly from the interface.

## Project Structure

```
veille-techno-backend/
├── src/
│   ├── auth/              # Registration, login, permissions
│   ├── users/             # User management
│   ├── lists/             # List management
│   ├── cards/             # Card management
│   ├── config/            # Configuration and environment validation
│   ├── app.module.ts
│   └── main.ts
│
├── test/                  # E2E and integration tests
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── users/
│   ├── lists/
│   └── cards/
│
├── .env                   # Local environment variables
├── .env.docker            # Docker environment variables
├── .env.example           # Example environment variables
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
└── README.md
```